/P 145 0 R
/E (Model Response: "A giraffe is a tall animal that lives in Africa. It has a long neck and legs, which help it reach high up into trees to eat leaves. Giraffes like to eat many kinds of plants, including leaves, flowers, and fruits. For instance, they love acacia leaves. Giraffes live in grassy places called savannas. One of their special characteristics is their spotted fur, which helps them hide from predators, like lions. Giraffes have babies called calves after being pregnant for 15 months. These calves can start walking soon after birth!)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
