4953 0 obj
<<
/Title (The water cycle is how water moves around the Earth. It has four main parts: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection. First, in evaporation, water from oceans, lakes, or rivers heats up and turns into a gas. This happens because the sun makes the water warm enough to rise into the air. Next is condensation. This means that water gas goes up high where it's colder. It then turns back into tiny drops, forming clouds. Then comes precipitation, which is when the water falls back to Earth. For example, it may fall as rain, snow, or hail. Precipitation happens because clouds get too heavy. Finally, in the collection part, the water goes back into rivers, lakes, and oceans. This is a cycle and therefore, it will start all over again!)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4933 0 R
>>
endobj
